From c8314ea3c97ebf0cb2c7556d5605f8453ef5daf5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Willian Z <willian@willian.email>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:13:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Let ZedLink connect open threads, reload project roots live
 and control queued messages

- allow_remote_attach (off by default): thread.attachable / thread.attach expose a thread open in a configured project from a paired device, with a desktop toast.
- Threads in SSH windows whose folders haven't loaded wait and are exposed once they match a configured root, from the phone or /remote-control.
- project_root/project_roots changes apply without restarting; removed roots stop exposing their threads.
- thread.queue.update: send now, set steer, edit text-only and remove any queued message through the desktop queue paths.
- /remote-control distinguishes an unconfigured project from an unavailable probe.
